## Key Concepts

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **ret2heap** | Place shellcode on the heap and jump to it |
| **Anti-exploit check** | Reads return address to block `0xb` prefix addresses |
| **`strdup()`** | Copies input to a predictable heap address |
| **Heap RWE** | Heap is executable on this binary — bytes can run as code |
| **Shellcode** | Raw machine code bytes that spawn a shell via syscall |
| **`int 0x80`** | x86 Linux syscall gate — no libc needed |
| **`struct.pack("<I", addr)`** | Packs address as 4 bytes little-endian |